KG42.register("clusters-c906266fc5860f8f29b419b5",{"id":"34-market_versus_price_scheduling::v142-d-CL003","paper":"34-market_versus_price_scheduling","label":"Main-grid scheduled exchange and deviation charges under the DMO allocation reference","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-CL003","label":"Main-grid scheduled exchange and deviation charges under the DMO allocation reference","market_meaning":"A microgrid, taking the DMO allocated quantity as the reference, selects the main-grid scheduled exchange subject to tie-line capacity and the islanded state. The default policy charges positive scheduled deviations and exempts negative deviations from penalty. The absolute-deviation penalty is retained as another scenario and is not applied at the same time as the default policy.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M01"],"market_types":["DEM"],"process_stages":["clearing","activation","settlement"],"scope_disposition":"conditional","scope_explanation":"The shared R003 provides only the allocated-quantity interface, and its change of role, from an upstream decision output to a downstream fixed reference, is retained. The one-sided penalty and the absolute-deviation scenario apply separately. The source's suggestion for selecting the congestion scenario still has no formal trigger condition. What is discussed here is the charge for scheduled deviation; it has not been extended to settlement of measured deviations.","assembly_status":"partial","boundary_rationale":"The boundary is entry into microgrid scheduled exchange under the given allocation reference and formation of the deviation-charge obligation. The execution chain and the payment chain jointly express the same incentive mechanism. Repeated deviation definitions and selection constraints are retained as multiple representations and are not counted as additional independent rules. Upstream bid allocation serves only as a shared interface.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R006","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Provides the operational representation of main-grid scheduled exchange, the capacity and islanding conditions, and the deviation policy."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R010","ownership":"primary","role":"support","rationale":"Supplements the deviation-charge obligation and the basis of the coefficients. Its repeated deviation mathematics and its association with R006 are retained and are not treated as an added mechanism."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R003","ownership":"shared","role":"interface","rationale":"Cites only the DMO allocation output as the reference for scheduled deviation, and does not turn the DMO disaggregation objective, or all of the constraints, into the microgrid objective and the execution conditions."}],"connections":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-CON008","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R006","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R003::x::v141-c-R003-x-PDM","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C006"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R006::theta::v141-c-R006-T001","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C004"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e003","v141-b-g01-e022","v141-b-g01-e027","v141-b-g01-e034","v141-b-g01-e035"],"rationale":"The source uses the allocated quantity of each microgrid calculated by the DMO as the reference for scheduled-exchange deviation. In the allocation chain it is an output variable, and in the microgrid problem it is a fixed input. The roles are retained separately."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CON009","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R006","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R010","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R006::x::v141-c-R006-X001","v141-c-R006::x::v141-c-R006-X003","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C004"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C001","v141-c-R010::theta::theta_nu_penalty"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e018","v141-b-g01-e025","v141-b-g01-e026","v141-b-g01-e027"],"rationale":"The selected quantity of positive scheduled deviation enters the deviation charge in the dispatch objective, and the payment chain records its charge obligation and the basis of the coefficients. This supports functional coupling between the planning decision and the economic incentive."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CON010","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R006","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R010","kind":"alternative_representation","from_refs":["v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C004"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C001","v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C004","v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C005"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e018","v141-b-g01-e022","v141-b-g01-e023","v141-b-g01-e024","v141-b-g01-e025","v141-b-g01-e027"],"rationale":"R006 combines the deviation definition, the selection constraints, and the charge term in one object, whereas R010 records them in split form. Only the whole-group representations are associated here. It is not claimed that any one split constraint, taken alone, equals the entire combined object. Differences in the capacity subscripts continue to be retained."}],"object_mappings":[{"mapping_id":"v142-d-OM004","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R003::x::v141-c-R003-x-PDM","v141-c-R006::theta::v141-c-R006-T001","v141-c-R010::theta::theta_pdm_assigned"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e003","v141-b-g01-e022","v141-b-g01-e027","v141-b-g01-e034","v141-b-g01-e035"],"rationale":"Both refer to the DMO allocated quantity of the same microgrid in the same hour. The different local roles of the allocation decision variable and the deviation-calculation parameter are retained. The downstream MW annotation is not used to rewrite the unit that R003 does not specify."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-OM005","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R006::x::v141-c-R006-X001","v141-c-R010::x::x_pm_scheduled"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e003","v141-b-g01-e021","v141-b-g01-e022","v141-b-g01-e027"],"rationale":"The definition in the same mechanism and the deviation equation jointly support that both are the microgrid main-grid scheduled-exchange quantity. The capacity constraint on the execution side and the role of use on the charge side are retained separately."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-OM006","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R006::x::v141-c-R006-X002","v141-c-R010::x::x_delta_pm_deviation"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e022","v141-b-g01-e027"],"rationale":"Both are defined by the difference between the same scheduled-exchange quantity and the DMO allocated quantity. The indices and the mechanism scope agree, and each object and its use are retained."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-OM007","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R006::x::v141-c-R006-X003","v141-c-R010::x::x_delta_pm_positive"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e018","v141-b-g01-e023","v141-b-g01-e024","v141-b-g01-e027"],"rationale":"Under the same one-sided policy, the positive-deviation selected quantities serve the scheduling constraint and the charge term respectively. The same-quantity association does not remove the boundary problem in the selection mathematics."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-OM008","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R006::x::v141-c-R006-X004","v141-c-R010::x::x_delta_indicator"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e003","v141-b-g01-e023","v141-b-g01-e024","v141-b-g01-e027"],"rationale":"The source definition and the selection constraints of the same group support this as the same binary deviation indicator. The original domains and explanations of both chains are retained."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-OM009","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R006::theta::v141-c-R006-T002","v141-c-R010::theta::theta_nu_penalty"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e004","v141-b-g01-e018","v141-b-g01-e025"],"rationale":"Both are the microgrid penalty coefficient in the default positive-deviation charge term. A market price, or a larger value, is only a qualitative basis. A numerical value is not set on that basis, and the coefficient is not automatically extended to the absolute-deviation scenario."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-OM010","kind":"alternative_representation","member_refs":["v141-c-R006::theta::v141-c-R006-T003","v141-c-R010::theta::theta_pm_max"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e021","v141-b-g01-e023","v141-b-g01-e024","v141-b-g02-E10"],"rationale":"Both places use the main-grid exchange upper bound in the relevant constraints, but the source transcription and the frozen representation differ in retention of the microgrid subscript, and the sufficiency of applying the capacity bound and the deviation-selection bound has not been confirmed. They are provisionally retained as representations pending verification."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-OM011","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R006::theta::v141-c-R006-T005","v141-c-R010::theta::theta_epsilon"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e024"],"rationale":"Both correspond to the same small positive offset in Eq. (10). The numerical value that is not given remains unknown. The constraint-side object and the charge-implementation-side object are retained."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-OM012","kind":"alternative_representation","member_refs":["v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C005","v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C002"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e023","v141-b-g01-e024","v141-b-g01-e025","v141-b-g01-e027"],"rationale":"Both express the policy that negative deviations are exempt from penalty, but the form in R006 includes the zero point and the conclusion on the indicator, whereas R010 uses a strictly negative-deviation condition. The boundary and the range expressed differ, so a single constraint cannot be selected to replace both."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-OM013","kind":"alternative_representation","member_refs":["v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C006","v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C003"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E29","v141-b-g03-e03","v141-b-g03-e08","v141-b-g03-e09"],"rationale":"Both point to the same absolute-deviation penalty scenario, emphasizing respectively the behavioral consequence of following the schedule and the billing base quantity. Each expression and role is retained, and they are not equated with the default one-sided policy."}],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-G008","category":"unverified_source","description":"None of the citations has yet undergone an independent source audit. In particular, the candidate transcription of Eq. (10) contains deviation signs, whereas the signs presented by the existing anchors are inconsistent. The original-page image has not been checked at present.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R003","v141-c-R006","v141-c-R010"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R003::x::v141-c-R003-x-PDM","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C004","v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C005"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e022","v141-b-g01-e024","v141-b-g01-e025","v141-b-g01-e027","v141-b-g01-e034","v141-b-g02-E10","v141-b-g02-E29"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Subsequently verify, against the original page, the deviation signs of Eq. (10), the upper-bound subscripts, and the text of each scenario. This round keeps the C mathematics unchanged and does not claim that the transcription has been verified."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-G009","category":"math_incomplete","description":"Under the current Eqs. (8)-(10), and with ε positive, there is no feasible selection branch when the positive deviation is less than ε, and the non-positive branch is also jointly truncated by the capacity and ε. Using tie-line capacity directly as the deviation-selection bound has not been shown to cover the full possible range of scheduled exchange minus allocated quantity. The textual policy and the feasible region cannot be regarded as fully consistent.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R006","v141-c-R010"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C004","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C005","v141-c-R006::theta::v141-c-R006-T003","v141-c-R006::theta::v141-c-R006-T005","v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C002","v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C005","v141-c-R010::theta::theta_pm_max","v141-c-R010::theta::theta_epsilon"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e021","v141-b-g01-e022","v141-b-g01-e023","v141-b-g01-e024","v141-b-g01-e027"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Confirm the use of ε, the treatment near zero, and the feasible region of the allocation reference, and verify whether the deviation-selection bound is sufficient. If revision is needed, it is handled upstream. D does not rewrite the existing constraints."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-G010","category":"upstream_missing","description":"The frozen chains cover only the main-grid interface and the deviation charges. They do not include microgrid balance, DER constraints, or the remaining terms of objective (1), and they cannot serve as a complete microgrid dispatch model. It is also not yet clear whether the summation over i in objective (1) counts the deviation charge more than once, or what the charge unit and the period length are.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R006","v141-c-R010"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C002","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C004","v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e017","v141-b-g01-e018","v141-b-g01-e019","v141-b-g01-e020","v141-b-g01-e026"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"B/C is to verify the complete microgrid objective, the constraints, and the counting of charges. Until the frozen chains are supplemented, this cluster maintains the limited scope of the main-grid interface and the deviation charges and does not add a total-charge formula."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-G011","category":"math_incomplete","description":"The absolute-deviation scenario has only a penalty base quantity and a behavioral description. It lacks an explicit coefficient, a charge expression, and conditions for selecting the regime. The source attributes the selection to the distribution system operator, but the correspondence of that entity with the DMO is not yet clear, and no congestion-trigger threshold is given.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R006","v141-c-R010"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C006","v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E29","v141-b-g03-e03","v141-b-g03-e08","v141-b-g03-e09"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Verify the coefficient and charge of the absolute-deviation scenario, and the entity that makes the selection and the conditions of that selection. Do not automatically reuse the coefficient of the one-sided regime or apply both regimes at the same time."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-G012","category":"ontology_extension","description":"The deviation charge is currently attached to execution.energy_trade and settlement.payment. What the source describes is scheduled-deviation cost. It does not provide complete transaction payment or settlement of measured deviations. The two proposals for deviation-penalty nodes remain pending and cannot be used as approved nodes.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R006","v141-c-R010"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R006::V::execution.energy_trade","v141-c-R010::V::settlement.payment","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C004","v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e018","v141-b-g01-e025","v141-b-g01-e026","v141-b-g03-e02","v141-b-g03-e03"],"proposal_ids":["v141-b-g01-p001","proposal:v141-b-g03-deviation_penalty"],"required_work":"Manually compare the overlap of the two pending proposals and the semantic boundary between scheduled-deviation cost and transaction payment. Retain the frozen attachment and the pending status, and do not insert new nodes in D."}]},"rule_refs":["34-market_versus_price_scheduling::v141-c-R006","34-market_versus_price_scheduling::v141-c-R010","34-market_versus_price_scheduling::v141-c-R003"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-02e3a33daeacdc8d","COMP-234e316a4df6b1c7","COMP-88724c482f4695e1","COMP-c1310ff0c42d5a65","KG40-fe5714e5a1d65999"]});
